+Provisioning & rotating KMS keys (operator notes)
+-----------------------------------------------
+
+This directory contains helper guidance for provisioning and rotating AWS KMS keys used for cosign signing.
+
+Steps (operator):
+1. Provision a new KMS key (recommended via terraform in ../kms_and_s3 or your org IaC process).
+2. If creating a replacement key for rotation, capture the new KMS ARN.
+3. Update Kubernetes secret containing the cosign KMS ARN:
+     kubectl -n security create secret generic cosign-kms --from-literal=kms_arn=<NEW_ARN> --dry-run=client -o yaml | kubectl apply -f -
+4. Update CI secret (GitHub Actions) with the new KMS key ARN:
+     gh secret set COSIGN_AWS_KMS_KEY_ARN --body "<NEW_ARN>" --repo <org/repo>
+5. Optionally re-sign latest artifacts (or let CI re-sign on next build).
+
+Notes:
+- Do not delete the old KMS key immediately — keep until old signatures expire or until you re-sign historical artifacts.
+- For HSM-backed keys, consult cloud provider docs (AWS CloudHSM vs AWS KMS with custom key store).
+
